[E-INSTANCE-HEAD] Error: an instance must be for a type name applied to distinct variables, like `Pretty (List a)`; `Pretty (List (List Nat))` isn't
    ╭─[ reject/instance-head-synonym.sw:14:10 ]
    │
 14 │ instance Pretty.instGrid: Pretty Grid :=
    │          ───────┬───────  
    │                 ╰───────── an instance must be for a type name applied to distinct variables, like `Pretty (List a)`; `Pretty (List (List Nat))` isn't
    │ 
    │ Note 1: so two instances of one interface overlap exactly when they're for the same type name; use a named alternative (a `def` of the interface's type, passed by name) for anything more specific
    │ 
    │ Note 2: `Grid` is another name for a type, and the instance is for that type
────╯
